WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.340
- Moving sucks.
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:03.980
You know, strangers
handling your belongings,

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:05.680
the movers always break something.

00:00:08.832 --> 00:00:10.520
So that's gonna be first
month and last month rent,

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:11.840
one month security deposit.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:13.383
I'll get the paperwork started.

00:00:14.404 --> 00:00:16.300
(music continues)

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:18.120
So I have finished the kitchen.

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:19.060
I have finished my bedroom.

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:20.600
I have finished the office

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:22.250
and I'm just wrapping up the living room.

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:23.083
- Okay.

00:00:23.083 --> 00:00:24.310
So I'll get pack-a-lacking.

00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:25.143
- I love it, I love it.

00:00:25.143 --> 00:00:26.460
- Mind if I put on some music?

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.440
- I do not, I do not.
All right.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:30.540
- I got this new dub step.

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:31.627
- Dub step- what is that?

00:00:31.627 --> 00:00:32.530
I don't know what that is.

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:33.702
- Oh, dude.

00:00:33.702 --> 00:00:34.535
You're gonna love it.

00:00:34.535 --> 00:00:35.368
- Oh, cool, cool man.

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:38.868
(dup step plays)

00:00:38.868 --> 00:00:40.307
I like this.

00:00:40.307 --> 00:00:41.485
- Wait for the drop.

00:00:41.485 --> 00:00:42.932
- I'm sorry, the drop?

00:00:42.932 --> 00:00:45.349
(beat drops)

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:54.684
What is happening?

00:00:54.684 --> 00:00:55.675
- What?

00:00:55.675 --> 00:00:57.503
- What is this?

00:00:57.503 --> 00:00:59.433
I can't hear you talk.

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:01.483
What is that?

00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:03.910
- The music?

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:05.190
- I'm sorry, is that music?

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:06.023
- Oh yeah.

00:01:06.023 --> 00:01:07.480
Dude, that's the dub step, man.

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:08.980
That's my jam.

00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:12.330
- Well, it's a little
loud, and disorienting,

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:13.163
and, you know,

00:01:13.163 --> 00:01:14.710
you're being a little
rough with my things.

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:15.543
- Rough with it?

00:01:15.543 --> 00:01:17.150
Dude, your stuff is fine.

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:18.790
- Why am I sweating so much?

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:20.600
- Because you're feeling it.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:21.670
- Is that a good thing?

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:23.580
- Yes.

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:25.714
Come on man, just give it another shot.

00:01:25.714 --> 00:01:28.433
- Okay, okay, I will.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.417
(dub step music resumes)

00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:54.160
- Whoa, dude, you're
totally jacking my flow up.

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:56.593
- Dude, your nose is
bleeding and so is mine.

00:01:57.570 --> 00:01:58.900
- Awesome.

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:01.000
- It doesn't really seem like music to me.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:05.080
- Okay, wow, Wali
getting a little bit old.

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:06.808
- No, don't do that.
All right.

00:02:06.808 --> 00:02:07.641
Come on.
No.

00:02:07.641 --> 00:02:08.779
Didn't realize that, okay.

00:02:08.779 --> 00:02:10.500
Yeah, what would you rather listen to?

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:12.260
I can hook you up with some
"Hootie and the Blowfish"

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:13.093
if that's your-

00:02:13.093 --> 00:02:14.310
- Oh, that's funny.
- Is that good?

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:15.490
Want some "Color Me Bad?"

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:16.780
- You know what, go ahead.

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:17.613
I don't care.

00:02:17.613 --> 00:02:18.540
I see what you're doing.

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:19.410
Go ahead and play it.

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:21.420
I don't care because I'm not that old.

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:23.270
I can get into it, okay.

00:02:23.270 --> 00:02:26.117
Let's just get the stuff packed, play it.

00:02:26.117 --> 00:02:29.534
(dup step music resumes)

00:02:52.662 --> 00:02:53.739
Ahh!

00:02:53.739 --> 00:02:54.822
- Ah, ah!

00:02:54.822 --> 00:02:58.343
(car alarm blares)

00:02:58.343 --> 00:03:00.075
- I think I'm getting it.

00:03:00.075 --> 00:03:00.908
- Yeah!

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:06.173
- Oh, thank you.

00:03:06.173 --> 00:03:08.040
- I wish I could just stay at my old place

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:09.810
but I can't afford the new rent.

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:10.900
- Yeah, moving sucks.

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:13.760
You know, strangers
handling your belongings,

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:15.290
the movers always break something.

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:18.020
- Oh, no, I can't afford
professional movers.

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:19.632
I'm moving myself this Saturday.

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:21.057
(suspenseful music)
(speech warps)

00:03:21.057 --> 00:03:21.890
- I'm going to do most of the small stuff

00:03:21.890 --> 00:03:24.090
just going back and
forth with my hatchback.

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:26.224
Oh, do you think you can
borrow your roommate's van,

00:03:26.224 --> 00:03:27.057
(speech returns to normal)
so you can help me with

00:03:27.057 --> 00:03:28.133
some of the big stuff?

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:39.290
- Yeah, you know what?

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:40.890
I've been thinking a lot lately

00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:43.623
and I think we need to
spend some time apart.

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:46.120
Not to break up.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:48.523
No, just some time,

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:52.660
time apart to figure ourselves out

00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:56.773
and then we come back
together stronger, you know?

00:03:56.773 --> 00:03:58.980
- This is coming outta nowhere.

00:03:58.980 --> 00:03:59.960
- No, it's not.

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:02.593
I've tried to tell you like a,

00:04:02.593 --> 00:04:05.480
like a million different ways,

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:07.017
but you, you don't listen, see?

00:04:07.017 --> 00:04:09.520
That's the thing is that you never listen.

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:11.820
I don't need this time apart for me.

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:13.720
I need this time apart for us.

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:15.880
How long do you think it's
gonna take you to move?

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:17.690
- Okay, this is about the move.

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:19.100
You don't wanna help me move.

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:19.933
- What?

00:04:21.078 --> 00:04:22.900
I would love to help you move.

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:25.420
That's what boyfriends do, Claire.

00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:27.460
- I just think that
it's a weird coincidence

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:30.060
that you need space right
when I'm about to move.

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:31.710
- Oh my God.

00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:33.170
Oh my God.

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:34.820
I am so sorry

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:39.670
that I didn't plan my emotional
turmoil around your move.

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:40.920
Look at your face, see?

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:43.570
And now you've assumed the worst of me,

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:44.610
because you do that.

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:47.820
And that's why we need to spend
time apart from each other.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:50.250
- That is not fair.

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:52.070
- Not fair?

00:04:52.070 --> 00:04:57.070
Babe, all I'm asking for is
12 lousy hours this Saturday.

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:59.610
- Okay, fine!

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:00.443
- Okay, fine?

00:05:01.476 --> 00:05:04.520
- We'll move on Sunday.
- 48 hours.

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:05.840
I don't know what I was thinking.

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:10.400
12 hours is nowhere near enough time

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:13.260
to do what I need to do

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:15.790
to make our relationship stronger.

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:19.900
See, you got me all
confused and you know what?

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:21.560
I love you, but I gotta get outta here.

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:22.393
I can't.

00:05:22.393 --> 00:05:23.378
I just can't.

00:05:23.378 --> 00:05:24.211
I don't-

00:05:24.211 --> 00:05:25.044
I'm so confused right now.
(phone dings)

00:05:25.044 --> 00:05:25.877
I feel-

00:05:25.877 --> 00:05:26.720
I can't think,

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:28.470
and the walls are closing in on me

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:30.060
and I just don't know what to do.

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:31.233
- That was my landlord.

00:05:32.270 --> 00:05:34.000
He says he doesn't want
to lose me as a tenant

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.573
so he is not going to raise my rent.

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:39.533
Now I don't have to leave my place.

00:05:41.065 --> 00:05:41.960
- And I don't need
(romantic music swells)

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:44.793
time and apart because
we're perfect together.

00:05:48.446 --> 00:05:49.946
Will you marry me?

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:54.270
- You paint my apartment.

00:05:55.770 --> 00:05:56.667
- Yeah, of course, I'm
painting your apartment.

00:05:56.667 --> 00:05:58.310
That's what boyfriends do.

00:05:58.310 --> 00:06:00.523
When exactly do you think
that's gonna happen?

00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:03.440
- What are we doing in this neighborhood?

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:05.880
- Come on, this place
is in our price range.

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:06.713
Besides, I mean,

00:06:06.713 --> 00:06:08.874
people say the neighborhood's
turning around.

00:06:08.874 --> 00:06:11.420
- [Devon] Who the (beep) there?

00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:12.950
- It's Jordan and Kira.

00:06:12.950 --> 00:06:15.563
We're here to view the apartment at three.

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:21.210
- Oh (beep) my bad.

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:23.030
I had this homeless crack head

00:06:23.030 --> 00:06:25.340
trying to set up house in here yesterday,

00:06:25.340 --> 00:06:27.095
almost had to beat his ass.

00:06:27.095 --> 00:06:28.540
But y'all ain't got nothing to worry about

00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:30.340
'cause anybody try to get up in here

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:31.593
I will murder them.

00:06:32.550 --> 00:06:34.510
Let me give y'all the tour.

00:06:34.510 --> 00:06:36.670
All right, so we got
these vintage windows.

00:06:36.670 --> 00:06:39.415
They been here as long as
the building been here.

00:06:39.415 --> 00:06:40.700
(beep) get away from the window,

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:41.955
(tires screech)
get away from the window!

00:06:41.955 --> 00:06:42.788
Hey, Hey!

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:45.773
You mother-(beep) I see you out there.

00:06:45.773 --> 00:06:48.541
You get out that car
and I will murder you.

00:06:48.541 --> 00:06:51.228
(tires speed off)
That's what I thought.

00:06:51.228 --> 00:06:54.728
Roll on, (beep), roll on.

00:06:55.894 --> 00:06:58.043
My nephew Craig.

00:06:58.043 --> 00:06:59.093
He a good kid.

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:01.450
He smoke crack though.

00:07:05.501 --> 00:07:07.920
Just in case he turns back.

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:09.260
I filed the serial number off there

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:10.810
so if you got to shoot anybody,

00:07:10.810 --> 00:07:13.407
just make sure to wipe your
fingerprints off this (beep).

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:15.896
Well, come on, y'all,

00:07:15.896 --> 00:07:17.910
I ain't gonna bite you.

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:18.923
Brand new cupboards.

00:07:19.950 --> 00:07:22.080
I put the contact paper in myself here

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:24.287
so y'all don't get no germs.

00:07:24.287 --> 00:07:25.120
Get down!

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:31.623
Nah, ain't no thing.

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:34.720
I thought Craig was rolling back.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:37.180
I ain't getting shot by this
mother(beep) twice, damn.

00:07:37.180 --> 00:07:38.320
While we down here,

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:41.700
check this out, original hardwood floor

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:43.670
from when the building was built.

00:07:43.670 --> 00:07:45.920
Check out this grain, brother.

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:47.730
Ooh, that is craftsmanship.

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:48.563
Anyway, come on.

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:54.513
This paint is all new.

00:07:55.643 --> 00:07:58.380
Oh, (beep)

00:07:58.380 --> 00:08:01.270
Okay, this happened after I had painted.

00:08:01.270 --> 00:08:02.260
Funny story,

00:08:02.260 --> 00:08:04.070
we got crack heads in this neighborhood

00:08:04.070 --> 00:08:06.210
and one of 'em living right
next door here, right?

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:07.610
And one day he was smoking crack,

00:08:07.610 --> 00:08:10.340
just went Looney Toons and
mistook his nine millimeter,

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:12.930
that's a pistol honey,
for the remote control.

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:13.763
But don't worry.

00:08:13.763 --> 00:08:15.330
You ain't never gonna see him again.

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:20.543
Ain't nobody ever going to see him again.

00:08:24.910 --> 00:08:26.700
Plus, I'm gonna put a
fancy little hook in there

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:28.410
and turn that into a hat wrack.

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:30.233
Let's take a look at this bedroom.

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:32.890
What the (beep)?

00:08:32.890 --> 00:08:34.736
- I found this place first!

00:08:34.736 --> 00:08:35.569
- Found it?

00:08:35.569 --> 00:08:36.730
Man, I own this place.

00:08:36.730 --> 00:08:38.032
Can y'all gimme a second?

00:08:38.032 --> 00:08:40.902
(Devon and squatter fighting)

00:08:40.902 --> 00:08:43.187
You gonna bite me, mother(beep)?

00:08:43.187 --> 00:08:45.535
I will cut you with my sword cane.

00:08:45.535 --> 00:08:48.618
(fighting continues)

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:53.680
So that's gonna be first
month and last month rent,

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:54.980
one month security deposit,

00:08:54.980 --> 00:08:56.530
I'll get the paperwork started.

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:03.523
- Okay, baby, let's hit
this rock real quick.

00:09:07.110 --> 00:09:08.560
- [Devon] It's your landlord.

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:11.483
- Hey Devon.

00:09:12.773 --> 00:09:14.450
- Hey, how you doing brother?

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:15.283
How you doing?

00:09:15.283 --> 00:09:18.590
Yeah, just stopping by.

00:09:18.590 --> 00:09:21.253
Just wanted to check up on everything.

00:09:23.740 --> 00:09:25.830
- Okay.
Ah-ha!

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:28.760
You in here you little mother(beep)?

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:29.593
Nope.

00:09:30.590 --> 00:09:31.573
Closet look good.

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:35.233
Door is strong.

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:37.600
So y'all settling in?

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:40.450
- Yeah, we've been living
here a year and a half.

00:09:40.450 --> 00:09:41.850
So we have.

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:45.460
- So how these cupboards
working out for you?

00:09:46.590 --> 00:09:49.410
Nobody in here besides your stuff,

00:09:49.410 --> 00:09:50.960
which looks good.
- Thank you.

00:09:52.060 --> 00:09:53.643
Completely unrelated,

00:09:53.643 --> 00:09:56.440
have y'all seen a four foot 11 dude

00:09:56.440 --> 00:09:57.850
with a purple beard up in here.

00:09:57.850 --> 00:09:59.640
- No, no.

00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:03.943
No one's in here probably
because we lock the door.

00:10:04.889 --> 00:10:07.498
- Oh, he got the body like a rat.

00:10:07.498 --> 00:10:11.263
He can just squeeze through the vents.

00:10:12.592 --> 00:10:15.060
- Yeah, so you think somebody's
hiding in my apartment?

00:10:15.060 --> 00:10:16.170
- No.

00:10:16.170 --> 00:10:19.170
I told you, it's just a social call.

00:10:19.170 --> 00:10:20.120
I mean, why would Gerald

00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:22.360
be in here anyway.
- Gerald?

00:10:22.360 --> 00:10:24.880
There's a man, with a purple beard,

00:10:24.880 --> 00:10:27.340
named Gerald in my apartment?

00:10:27.340 --> 00:10:28.240
- Hell no.

00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:29.073
Why?

00:10:29.073 --> 00:10:30.110
Did you see him?

00:10:30.110 --> 00:10:32.340
He about four foot nine,
got a purple beard.

00:10:32.340 --> 00:10:33.729
- Yeah.
- Hey, baby-

00:10:33.729 --> 00:10:38.729
- Ah!
(Kira screams)

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:43.600
Oh, hey baby girl.

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:44.450
You ain't Gerald.

00:10:45.960 --> 00:10:46.793
Oh, by the by,

00:10:46.793 --> 00:10:49.550
have you seen a four
foot five purple beard?

00:10:49.550 --> 00:10:50.670
- Baby.

00:10:50.670 --> 00:10:52.663
- Devon, what's going on?

00:10:53.690 --> 00:10:55.880
- Okay, you know what I'm
gonna level with y'all,

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:57.720
there is a four foot three (beep)

00:10:57.720 --> 00:10:59.450
with a purple beard named Gerald

00:10:59.450 --> 00:11:01.340
somewhere in this building.

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:03.270
- Why does he keep getting smaller

00:11:03.270 --> 00:11:04.450
every time you mention him?

00:11:04.450 --> 00:11:05.283
- Seriously?

00:11:05.283 --> 00:11:07.130
Cause I didn't wanna alarm y'all.

00:11:07.130 --> 00:11:10.470
He is disturbingly small, really.

00:11:10.470 --> 00:11:12.120
He's a good guy.

00:11:12.120 --> 00:11:13.520
He smoke rock though.

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:17.453
I mean, he'll do anything
to get money for crack.

00:11:18.550 --> 00:11:20.363
Anything.
- Okay.

00:11:21.210 --> 00:11:22.743
- I mean anything.

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:25.203
- I get it.

00:11:25.203 --> 00:11:30.000
- He will murder you.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:34.050
- Well, we certainly hope you find him.

00:11:34.050 --> 00:11:36.180
- Oh, I'm gonna find him.

00:11:36.180 --> 00:11:37.940
Don't worry about that

00:11:37.940 --> 00:11:39.730
because I'm gonna look low

00:11:39.730 --> 00:11:41.760
and then I'm gonna look high.

00:11:45.016 --> 00:11:45.849
- Ah!

00:11:46.710 --> 00:11:49.686
(Jordan and Kira scream)

00:11:49.686 --> 00:11:52.400
- Gerald, you tiny little bitch!

00:11:52.400 --> 00:11:54.220
Sorry for the inconvenience, y'all.

00:11:54.220 --> 00:11:55.614
Gerald, when I get my hands on you,

00:11:55.614 --> 00:11:57.022
you're gonna be two foot three.

00:11:57.022 --> 00:11:58.257
(door slams)

00:11:58.257 --> 00:12:00.840
(upbeat music)

